<article class="env-lemma" id="036B">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/036B">Lemma <span data-tag="036B">35.17.2</span>.</a> The property $\mathcal{P}(S) =$“$S$ is Cohen-Macaulay” is local in the syntomic topology. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is clear from Lemma <a href="/tag/036A" data-tag="036A">35.17.1</a> above since a scheme is Cohen-Macaulay if and only if it is locally Noetherian and $(S_ k)$ for all $k \geq 0$, see Properties, Lemma <a href="/tag/0342" data-tag="0342">28.12.3</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>